this is a temper in a simple rectangle  segmented into ten equal sized boxes in  two rows of five a ten frame is a tool  that is designed to encourage  kindergarten and first-grade students to  understand numbers in relation to the  number ten and organize physical items  they will be counting ten is important  because it is the base of our number  system we only write with a numeral x'  zero through nine so to indicate the  next larger counting number beyond nine  we must write our numerals in a new  place known as the tens place when we  have a group of ten ones or in other  words when we fill our 10 frame we  recognize that we have enough to bundle  the group into a new value indicated by  placing a numeral one in the position to  the left of the ones place known as the  tens place this is the beginning phase  for understanding place value to learn  more about the development of place  value in Singapore math please watch the  short video on the place value chart in  the early stages of the development of  numbers encourage your child to build a  given quantity or show you a specific  number of items from zero to ten such as  show me for the child would then place  the counters on the tenth frame one two  three four there we go  in this example I am using the two  colored counters which are red on one  side and yellow on the other but you  could use small and large buttons or  different types of dry beans really  whatever you have lying around the house  also drawing your own 10 frame to use  with your child is really quick and easy  to do later you will develop the  concepts of addition and subtraction by  asking him to add or subtract some  amount you could say something like now  add three more and tell me how many  there are they would then place three  more counters on the  frame and let you know that there are  now seven counters or buttons or beans  as you work with your child is important  to consistently refer to the number ten  understanding numbers and each numbers  relationship to ten help students  develop strategies used in mental math  so questions such as how many more do we  need to make ten is really valuable to  better understand how this helps with  mental math please take a moment to  watch the video about number bonds  another great way to use the ten frame  is to ask the question how many  different ways can you make a number  such as seven doing this can help  develop a child's sense of what each  number can be made of this is also a  helpful way to start developing addition  and subtraction math facts through ten  and it leads well into the already  referenced number bonds which again I  discuss in another video but simply put  it is a picture representation of how to  break apart numbers into smaller  component parts thanks for watching and  please check out the other videos  available online
 

